Z||000014||LZeitgeist||12-09-2001||12:55 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Hey LZeitgeist, check out the part number on the side of the box that you got from me. Then ask those other guys what part number is on their $250 (wholesale price) clutch. Then you can go the the CForce web site <A HREF="http://www.centerforce.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.centerforce.com/</A>  and you'll find that the Clutch they make for me isn't even available to the general public yet. So there is actually no comparison between what they are talking about and what you have.<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Actually, I had already checked the part number on the side of the box vs. what I found on the Centerforce website, and I thought maybe the box was leftover from another application... wasn't worried about it, 'cuz you told me this was the best one for the job, and I trust ya.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>But <B>WOW!</B> - I had no idea this was actually the case.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Seems like my trust was well-placed in you. No complaints here whatsoever.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>(Not that I had any in any case - like I said, I feel it was money well-spent.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">)<P>(And if they want the part number, they're gonna have to get it from you, 'cuz I ain't talkin'!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">)<P>Thanks again, Archie... ||||reg||1
